      "conditions": null,
      "page": 3,
      "source_text": "ODSA is a mild primary skin irritant. Avoid contact with skin, eyes and clothing. Use only with adequate ventilation. In case of contact, immediately flush skin or eyes with plenty of water for at least 15 minutes; for eyes, get medical attention. Wash contaminated clothing before reuse."
    }
  ],
  "sections": [
    {
      "name": "Applications",
      "page": 2,
      "text": "ODSA is an alkenyl succinic anhydride (ASA) based on C18 alpha-olefin. This versatile molecule is often used as an alkaline paper sizing agent. ODSA is also used in fuel and lubricant additives including pour point depressants, corrosion inhibitors and dispersants. ASAs find use as intermediates for surfactants and can also be converted to acid amides and esters. Other suggested uses are in plasticizers, epoxies, and moisture control for leather goods."
    },
    {
      "name": "Registration",
      "page": 2,
      "text": "ODSA is REACh registered as a component under the name 2,5-Furandione,dihydro-,mono-C15-20-alkenyl derivs. The CASRN is 68784-12-3 and the REACh registry number is 01-2119533117-46. In the US, CASRN 28777-98-2 is typically used for ODSA."
    },
    {
      "name": "Handling & Storage",
      "page": 3,
      "text": "ODSA must be stored out of contact with moisture to avoid hydrolysis of the anhydride to the acid. When properly stored, ODSA has a shelf life of 24 months.\n\nFor more details on the design of bulk storage for ODSA and similar products, consult the Dixie Chemical brochure \"Alkenylsuccinic Anhydride Storage Requirements.\""
    },
    {
      "name": "Health Hazards",
      "page": 3,
      "text": "Read and understand the relevant Safety Data Sheets (SDS) for all products before use. ODSA is a mild primary skin irritant. Avoid contact with skin, eyes and clothing. Use only with adequate ventilation. In case of contact, immediately flush skin or eyes with plenty of water for at least 15 minutes; for eyes, get medical attention. Wash contaminated clothing before reuse."
    },
    {
      "name": "Availability",
      "page": 3,
      "text": "ODSA is available from Dixie Chemical in Pasadena, TX. Contact your Dixie representative for details."
    }
  ],
